    0: Metadata: Saint Vincent and The Grenadines
    1: Contents
    2: One metadata tab describing 3 geospatial boundary files and 7 tables, one data dictionary tab for 7 tables, and 7 tables ("Age-Sex," "Ethnicity and Religion," "Education and Occupation," "Households," "Buildings," "Access to Services," and "Info and Com Technology")
    3: Geospatial Boundary Metadata
    4: National Boundary (VC_GEOG_ADM0_2012_uscb_202109)
    5: Title | Saint Vincent and The Grenadines: National Boundary
    6: Tags | Geospatial Boundaries, Saint Vincent and The Grenadines, National Boundary, Country
    7: Summary | The U.S. Census Bureau is providing national and subnational feature class boundaries for joining to subnational population data for the USAID Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance.
    8: Description | National boundary feature class of Saint Vincent and The Grenadines for joining (linking) to attribute data provided in tables prepared by the U.S. Census Bureau.
    9: Credits | Source: Geospatial data for the national boundary of Saint Vincent and The Grenadines were downloaded from the DevInfo, available online at http://devinfo.org/ (no longer available online).

The U.S. Census Bureau cannot guarantee the accuracy of boundary placements.
    10: Use Limitations | The national boundaries used for this feature class were downloaded or derived from publicly available sources.
    11: Place Keywords | Saint Vincent and The Grenadines, Country
    12: Temporal Keywords | 2021
    13: Theme Keywords | National Boundaries
    14: Supplemental Information | The geodatabase feature class contains 1 polygon representing Saint Vincent and The Grenadines' national boundary.

Notes: 
(1) The original shapefile downloaded from DevInfo was misaligned with the shoreline for Saint Vincent and the Grenadines as represented in the ArcGIS basemap, but was corrected by USCB staff.
    15: First-Order Administrative Divisions (VC_GEOG_ADM1_2012_uscb_202109)
    16: Title | Saint Vincent and The Grenadines: First-Order Administrative Divisions
    17: Tags | Geospatial Boundaries, Saint Vincent and The Grenadines, First-Order Administrative Divisions, Census Division
    18: Summary | The U.S. Census Bureau is providing national and subnational feature class boundaries for joining to subnational population data for the USAID Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance.
    19: Description | First-order administrative divisions feature class of Saint Vincent and The Grenadines for joining (linking) to attribute data provided in tables prepared by the U.S. Census Bureau.
    20: Credits | Source: Geospatial data for the first-order administrative divisions of Saint Vincent and The Grenadines were downloaded from the Feasibility Study & Environmental Assessment for Georgetown Coastal Defense, Figure 3: Census Districts in Saint Vincent, available online at http://finance.gov.vc/finance/images/PDF/Publications/draft_env_ass_georgetown_2015.pdf (accessed July 08, 2021).

The U.S. Census Bureau cannot guarantee the accuracy of boundary placements.
    21: Use Limitations | The subnational boundaries used for this feature class were digitized by USCB staff from publicly available sources.
    22: Place Keywords | Saint Vincent and The Grenadines, Census Division
    23: Temporal Keywords | 2021
    24: Theme Keywords | Subnational Divisions
    25: Supplemental Information | The geodatabase feature class contains 13 polygons, 1 polygon for each of Saint Vincent and The Grenadines' first-order administrative divisions (census divisions), as reported by the Saint Vincent and The Grenadines Statistical Office.

Notes: 
(1) 2012 census materials utilized a 13 census division ADM1 structure that differs from the 6 parish ADM1 structure generally used in maps of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines. USCB utilized the 13 census division structure for the purposes of this product. For this reason, GENC and FIPS codes were not included in this product. The name of the parish that each enumeration district falls within is included in the PARISH field.
    26: Second-Order Administrative Divisions (VC_GEOG_ADM2_2012_uscb_202109)
    27: Title | Saint Vincent and The Grenadines: Second-Order Administrative Divisions
    28: Tags | Geospatial Boundaries, Saint Vincent and The Grenadines, Second-Order Administrative Divisions, Enumeration District
    29: Summary | The U.S. Census Bureau is providing national and subnational feature class boundaries for joining to subnational population data for the USAID Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance.
    30: Description | Second-order administrative divisions feature class of Saint Vincent and The Grenadines for joining (linking) to attribute data provided in tables prepared by the U.S. Census Bureau.
    31: Credits | Source: Geospatial data for the second-order administrative divisions of Saint Vincent and The Grenadines were downloaded from the Feasibility Study & Environmental Assessment for Georgetown Coastal Defense, Figure 3: Census Districts in Saint Vincent, available online at http://finance.gov.vc/finance/images/PDF/Publications/draft_env_ass_georgetown_2015.pdf (accessed July 08, 2021).

The U.S. Census Bureau cannot guarantee the accuracy of boundary placements.
    32: Use Limitations | The subnational boundaries used for this feature class were digitized by USCB staff from publicly available sources.
    33: Place Keywords | Saint Vincent and The Grenadines, Enumeration District
    34: Temporal Keywords | 2021
    35: Theme Keywords | Subnational Divisions
    36: Supplemental Information | The geodatabase feature class contains 221 polygons, 1 polygon for each of Saint Vincent and The Grenadines' second-order administrative divisions (enumeration districts), as reported by the Saint Vincent and The Grenadines Statistical Office.

Notes:
(1) Enumeration districts were used during the 2011 census and have no other administrative or government function in Saint Vincent and The Grenadines, but USCB are considering them to be ADM2 areas in order to provide more geographic detail for this product.
(2) A total of 221 enumeration districts were digitized by USCB staff. 196 enumeration districts for the island of Saint Vincent were digitized from the map found within the Feasibility Study & Environmental Assessment for Georgetown Coastal Defense. 25 enumeration districts for Northern and Southern Grenadines were digitized using Google Maps and OpenStreetMap.
(3) Original census materials included data for 333 enumeration districts. Data for some enumeration districts were combined by USCB staff to match the maps used to digitize the 221 ADM2 boundaries for this product. Areas with more than one enumeration district code in the NSO_CODE field were combined from the original census data by USCB.
